  "details": "Test World ID: https://www.vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_5f1e6ea8-6117-4587-9b4f-f9c1803408c8\nTesting in desktop mode.\nExpected behavior: Each player should be given a selection cursor and be able to click to place 5 spheres.\nIn this beta, the master is able to click to place spheres. However, anyone else who joins the world spawns an object at world origin, but is not given control of their own object.\nIt appears that an error is printed indicating that in this case, \"Lyuma 3f63\" is not the owner of the object it just spawned, instead \"Lyuma\" (the world master)\n    \n    2020.09.16 12:09:10 Log        -  [Network Processing] RPC invoked _InstantiateObject on SceneEventHandlerAndInstantiator for Lyuma 3f63\n    2020.09.16 12:09:10 Log        -  [ObjectInstantiator] Instantiated a (Clone [200004] SpawnedItem)\n    2020.09.16 12:09:10 Log        -  [Network Processing] RPC called SceneEventHandlerAndInstantiator:_SendOnSpawn:All and 8 bytes\n    2020.09.16 12:09:10 Log        -  [VRC_EventDispatcherRFC] Will execute SendRPC/AlwaysUnbuffered on SceneEventHandlerAndInstantiator (UnityEngine.GameObject) for Lyuma 3f63: S: \"_SendOnSpawn\" I: 0 F: 0 B: 255 (local non-master non-owner)\n    2020.09.16 12:09:10 Log        -  [Network Processing] RPC invoked _SendOnSpawn on SceneEventHandlerAndInstantiator for Lyuma 3f63\n    2020.09.16 12:09:10 Error      -  [ObjectInstantiator] Non-owner Lyuma 3f63 sent OnSpawn for 30D44, owner is Lyuma",
